1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Ainize: compile chain data into teachable provenance.
Real provider data becomes reviewable AI teaching inputs.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Discover a subgraph, inspect its schema, pin the query.
This recorded run uses Ethereum block 25969047.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:38,000
20 token records become 20 canonical question-and-answer rows.
The viewer shows two actual rows from the generated dataset.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Each row retains source, query and block provenance.
Reusable mapping prepares data for a separate teaching workflow.

5
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Authenticated upload to the running Ainize node: 20 accepted.
A real dataset ID and stored content hash come back.

6
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Stored SHA-256 matches the predicted dataset hash.
Dataset creation succeeded; no training or publication requested.

7
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Actual existing-model comparison on a DART address question.
Both answers contain the correct address, per team review.

8
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Base: 181 tokens / 3825 ms. Patched: 16 tokens / 759 ms.
One observation, not a statistical speedup or new Graph model.

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The DART patch remains REJECTED in the public catalogue.
Live testing is not verification for sale.

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
ENS registrar binds signed attestations to mint targets.
Changing the recipient, resolver or duration is refused.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Eight local security tests reported passing; source is included.
Sepolia deployment and live resolution are still pending.

12
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:25,000
